# Normalise line endings so the toolchain behaves the same on every machine.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, where Git's core.autocrlf=true converts
# files to CRLF on checkout. Prettier expects LF, so without this file a fresh
# clone fails `pnpm format:check` — one of the five mandatory verification
# commands — on every text file, before a line of code is written (BUG-099).
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` keeps LF in the repository AND in the working tree, which
# is what Prettier, ESLint and the test suite all assume.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary: never line-ending-converted, never diffed as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.avif  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary

# SVG is text (it diffs usefully and Prettier formats it), so it is covered by
# the `* text=auto eol=lf` rule above rather than being marked binary here.
